e data on visual impairment: A compilation of population-based prevalence studies</article-title><source>Ophthalmic Epidemiol</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>67</fpage><lpage>115</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15255026</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040086-b006"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group><name><surname>Mohamedain</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Prevalence survey of trachoma and its complications in Al-Ginena province</article-title><publisher-loc>Khartoum (Sudan)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>University of Khartoum</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040086-b007"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group><name><surname>Abusin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><source>Prevalence and causes of blindness in the Sudan: A review of published and unpublished data</source><publisher-loc>Khartoum (Sudan)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>University of Khartoum</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040086-b008"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Ngondi</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Onsarigo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Adamu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Matende</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Reacher</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The epidemiology of trachoma in Eastern Equatoria and Upper Nile States, southern Sudan</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><volume>83</volume><fpage>904</fpage><lpage>912</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16462982</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040086-b009"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Whitfield</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwab</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Ross-D